| ID | exact signal | decision | decisive reason |
|---|---|---|---|
| `R01/BSE` | For all tested `n=1,2,3`, including `m=1,2`, every orbit reaches a fixed point with the exact run-erasure tail.  Fixed counts, sharp parity-sensitive maximum tails, every target's transfer fibre, gap factorization, zero-target spectrum, and total fibre mass all match the closed formulas. | `PROVISIONAL_SURVIVOR_OWNER_AMBER` | Generic support/run erosion receives zero credit.  The residual package is stronger: natural Brandt sandwich multiplication, an all-parameter parity obstruction for the sharp tail, and an independent labelled-target inverse theory with an explicit local matrix spectrum.  Direct-owner status remains unresolved, so this is not numbered. |
| `R02/RBW` | For lengths `3..6`, tails are exactly `m-1`; first images halve the carrier and all nonempty first fibres have size two. | `KILL_DIRECT_SHIFT_REGISTER_THIN` | `(i,j)` multiplication only copies the next right coordinate.  Every theorem is a coordinate shift/projection, and rectangular-band cellular automata are established. |
| `R03/CSA` | Two fixed points in every box; maximum tails are `m` at cap two and `m+1` at cap three; indegrees are highly nonuniform. | `KILL_P108_PASCAL_CA_TRANSFER` | The closed iterate is capped Pascal convolution, the cyclic analogue of P108's capped Fibonacci engine.  The sharp clock is only an implicit cyclic-binomial threshold and the inverse axis never improved beyond a generic transfer matrix. |
| `R04/HUR` | Every state is recurrent; periods reach four on both `S_3` and `D_8`; all fibres have size one. | `KILL_DIRECT_HURWITZ_ACTION` | The literal update is a standard Hurwitz generator.  Finite-group specialization cannot claim its action or orbit language, and singleton fibres supply no independent axis. |
| `R05/CSW` | Pure fixed points and two-cycles; all fibres have size one. | `KILL_INVOLUTION_ACTION_ONLY` | The update is an involution because commutation is swap-invariant.  A commuting-pair census is static group theory, not a second dynamical theorem. |
| `R06/MGR` | `T^3=1`; `F_2^3` gives 344 fixed states and 56 three-cycles, while `F_3^3` gives 8,451 fixed states and 3,744 three-cycles; all fibres are one. | `KILL_RANK_GATE_ACTION_ONLY` | Rank merely gates identity versus cyclic coordinate rotation.  Gaussian full-rank counting plus a permutation action is below the value floor. |
| `R07/IAV` | Four constant fixed states; maximum tails `4,6,7,8` for lengths `3..6` at cap three; fibre histograms vary irregularly. | `KILL_CONSENSUS_OWNER_NO_INVERSE` | Integer floor averaging is in the consensus/quantized-averaging surface.  The sum Lyapunov function is not an exact all-parameter clock, and no independent labelled inverse law survived. |
| `R08/PFR` | All 5,461 words reach their ordinary reduced word; maximum parallel depth three; 1,457 fixed reduced words. | `KILL_DIRECT_FREE_REDUCTION` | Parallel deletion changes only the reduction schedule.  The normal form and inverse-word enumeration remain standard free-group rewriting, so the clock cannot support a paper. |
| `R09/RPX` | Rectangular bands `2x2` and `2x3` give only fixed points and two-cycles, with singleton fibres. | `KILL_PRODUCT_EXCHANGE_INVOLUTION` | The identity `(xy,yx)^2=(x,y)` is an immediate rectangular-band calculation.  This is thinner than already rejected group product-exchange systems. |
| `R10/BPA` | On `B_2^m`, recurrent count is always three, maximum tail is `m`, and the zero target dominates the fibre histogram. | `KILL_ZERO_PROPAGATION_NO_ATLAS` | Matrix-unit index mismatch merely propagates zero through local products.  Beyond the fixed diagonal words, no uniform target theorem independent of the compatibility-path engine emerged. |

## Final disposition

```text
candidate_denominator=10
survivors=1 (R01 provisional)
kills=9
paper_numbers_assigned=0
status=PROVISIONAL / OWNER_AMBER / HOLD_EXTERNAL / UNNUMBERED
